@*
    CodeBehindDemo.razor — markup only. The logic lives in the partial class
    CodeBehindDemo.razor.cs beside this file. Blazor will merge them at
    compile time thanks to the "partial" modifier.

    Use code-behind when:
      • The logic is long enough to clutter the @code block.
      • You want to unit-test the class without a renderer.
      • You want a class that inherits from a base component (ComponentBase).
*@

@page "/codebehind"
@rendermode InteractiveServer

<PageTitle>Code-behind</PageTitle>

<h1>Code-behind pattern</h1>

<p>
    Today's random lucky number is <strong>@lucky</strong>.
</p>

<button class="btn btn-primary" @onclick="Reroll">Reroll</button>
